  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"[P]rinted on Nideggen and Kitakata papers. The type is Walbaum, cast by Michael Bixler. The wood engravings, reproduced here from polymer plates, were made by M.L. Breton whose work appears in the 1863 edition of Dictionnaire Infernal published by Jacques Collin de Plancy ... Originally published in 1818, it was revised and reprinted several times. All design, [letterpress] printing and binding by Sandra and Harry Reese. The edition is 200 signed copies ..."--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Binding is Gary Frost's sewn board design in red cloth with paper over the front board which has same illustration as frontispiece, handcolored. Paper label with title inset into spine.</subfield>
  </datafield>
